{"bbox":[366.69001599999996,125.44161,504.794048,236.57109],"caption":"Figure 2: Distribution of QLIKE ratios (model / Log-HAR) across 50 assets. Values below one indicate the model outperforms Log-HAR. Boxes span the interquartile range; whiskers extend to 1.5× IQR; we suppress outliers. The dashed line marks parity with Log-HAR. The plot shows the competitive econometric benchmarks (HAR, ARFIMA, ARMA, MEM) alongside the foundation models. The augmented HAR variants (HAR-J, HAR-RS, HARQ) and Toto are excluded because their extreme per-asset QLIKE ratios (for example, HARQ has a median ratio near 1.9 and a maximum above 70) would compress the scale for the remaining models.","figure_id":"2026-brini-volatility-foundation-models:p0020:figure:0003","page_number":20,"paper_id":"2026-brini-volatility-foundation-models","provenance":{"extractor_name":"MinerU pipeline","extractor_version":"3.4.4","model_hash":"ed6b654c018d742e65a17671e379c5e6ecc87ec9","source_pdf_sha256":"1e017652c7f11eb9f5fc4f91f96bc26746425bb59937de333e4bc3aee2e47c1a"},"source_asset":"assets/figures/2026-brini-volatility-foundation-models-p0020-block-0004-ec994121c2d2c48a.jpg","source_bbox_normalized":[616,149,848,281],"source_block_id":"2026-brini-volatility-foundation-models:p0020:block:0004","verification_status":"unverified"}
{"bbox":[91.67250399999999,159.9591,504.794048,501.76644],"caption":"Figure 3: GR fluctuation test, by foundation model. Each panel plots the rolling Diebold–Mariano statistic (QLIKE loss) of one foundation model against Log-HAR, averaged across 50 assets, for the daily (h = 1), weekly (h = 5), and monthly (h = 22) horizons. Positive values indicate the model outperforms Log-HAR (lower QLIKE); negative values indicate Log-HAR is more accurate. Dashed horizontal lines mark the 5% critical values (±2.80); the window size is 30% of the sample. The TTM panel is highlighted.","figure_id":"2026-brini-volatility-foundation-models:p0023:figure:0001","page_number":23,"paper_id":"2026-brini-volatility-foundation-models","provenance":{"extractor_name":"MinerU pipeline","extractor_version":"3.4.4","model_hash":"ed6b654c018d742e65a17671e379c5e6ecc87ec9","source_pdf_sha256":"1e017652c7f11eb9f5fc4f91f96bc26746425bb59937de333e4bc3aee2e47c1a"},"source_asset":"assets/figures/2026-brini-volatility-foundation-models-p0023-block-0002-4de4f45695fe0319.jpg","source_bbox_normalized":[154,190,848,596],"source_block_id":"2026-brini-volatility-foundation-models:p0023:block:0002","verification_status":"unverified"}
{"bbox":[134.532376,150.69831,461.934176,505.97589],"caption":"Figure 4: QLIKE ratio (model / HAR) at $h = 1$ vs. first-order autocorrelation $\\rho _ { 1 }$ for 50 assets. Values below one indicate the foundation model outperforms HAR. Each point is one asset, colored by class (blue: equities, red: FX, green: futures). Dashed line: OLS trend; r and $p$ are the Pearson correlation and its p-value. Toto is omitted due to extreme QLIKE ratios on the commodity contracts. HAR (not Log-HAR) is used as the denominator so that the ratio is directly comparable to prior realized-volatility work, where HAR is the canonical baseline; using Log-HAR in its place shifts the ratio scale by a constant but does not change the cross-asset rank correlation with $\\rho _ { 1 }$","figure_id":"2026-brini-volatility-foundation-models:p0040:figure:0001","page_number":40,"paper_id":"2026-brini-volatility-foundation-models","provenance":{"extractor_name":"MinerU pipeline","extractor_version":"3.4.4","model_hash":"ed6b654c018d742e65a17671e379c5e6ecc87ec9","source_pdf_sha256":"1e017652c7f11eb9f5fc4f91f96bc26746425bb59937de333e4bc3aee2e47c1a"},"source_asset":"assets/figures/2026-brini-volatility-foundation-models-p0040-block-0002-bdaf143d56b253b3.jpg","source_bbox_normalized":[226,179,776,601],"source_block_id":"2026-brini-volatility-foundation-models:p0040:block:0002","verification_status":"unverified"}
{"bbox":[88.696124,129.65106,504.794048,405.79098],"caption":"Figure 5: Model Confidence Set inclusion for 50 assets. Green cells indicate that the model is included in the MCS at the 10% significance level (QLIKE loss). Left: $h = 1 ;$ center: $h = 5 ;$ right: $h = 2 2 .$ . The heatmap shows 15 of the 17 models; ARMA and MEM are omitted for space and their inclusion rates appear in Tab. 8.","figure_id":"2026-brini-volatility-foundation-models:p0041:figure:0001","page_number":41,"paper_id":"2026-brini-volatility-foundation-models","provenance":{"extractor_name":"MinerU pipeline","extractor_version":"3.4.4","model_hash":"ed6b654c018d742e65a17671e379c5e6ecc87ec9","source_pdf_sha256":"1e017652c7f11eb9f5fc4f91f96bc26746425bb59937de333e4bc3aee2e47c1a"},"source_asset":"assets/figures/2026-brini-volatility-foundation-models-p0041-block-0002-e4ac3fb801cffc92.jpg","source_bbox_normalized":[149,154,848,482],"source_block_id":"2026-brini-volatility-foundation-models:p0041:block:0002","verification_status":"unverified"}
